Chapter: ShellTextQuoting
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit
  cites Shell chapter BashEmit
  cites Shell chapter KshEmit

 SeText is the interpolating string node. It exists because SeLit is emitted
 SINGLE-quoted, so it cannot carry a $variable, and there was no other node --
 which is why 346 of the tree's escaped quotes were sitting inside SeRaw
 expression payloads holding a hand-quoted shell string.

 The arms that matter are the escaping ones, and the ORDER is the part that is
 easy to get wrong: escaping the quote before the escape character would then
 escape the character just inserted. Each emitter is asked directly rather than
 through a whole script, so a failure names the emitter.

 The dollar arm is the point of the node and is a control in the strict sense:
 if interpolation were escaped away the node would be pointless, so it must
 come through untouched.

 We say:

Section: Vectors

  plain : Text = "MISSING: nothing special"
  dollar : Text = "MISSING: $Stage0 - the -Kernel you asked for is not there"
  has-quote : Text = "he said \"no\" twice"
  has-backtick : Text = "a backtick ` here"
  has-backslash : Text = "path C:\\temp\\x"

Section: Body

  row : Text, Text -> Text
  row (label) (out) = label & " " & out

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (row "ps-plain    " (emit-ps-expr (msg plain)))
    print-line-uni (row "ps-dollar   " (emit-ps-expr (msg dollar)))
    print-line-uni (row "ps-quote    " (emit-ps-expr (msg has-quote)))
    print-line-uni (row "ps-backtick " (emit-ps-expr (msg has-backtick)))
    print-line-uni (row "ps-backslash" (emit-ps-expr (msg has-backslash)))
    print-line-uni (row "sh-dollar   " (emit-bash-expr (msg dollar)))
    print-line-uni (row "sh-quote    " (emit-bash-expr (msg has-quote)))
    print-line-uni (row "sh-backtick " (emit-bash-expr (msg has-backtick)))
    print-line-uni (row "sh-backslash" (emit-bash-expr (msg has-backslash)))
    print-line-uni (row "ksh-quote   " (emit-ksh-expr (msg has-quote)))
    print-line-uni (row "lit-still-sq" (emit-ps-expr (sh-lit dollar)))
  end
